A set named after the type it builds ("server" for *Server) gives the injector's
result and local variables the base name "server", equal to the generated
function name. On regeneration the re-scanned output file must not reserve that
name for the local allocator, so re-running plumb over its own output reproduces
it byte-for-byte instead of drifting to a suffixed name.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Server struct{}

//plumb:server
func NewServer() *Server { return &Server{} }
